/-
The Iwasawa disintegration of the rational-centre-unipotent quotient measure.

Let `K` be a number field, `Z(K)·U(K) = rationalCentreUnipotent K` the closed subgroup of
`AdelicGL2 (𝓞 K) K` generated by the central scalars `centralScalar (𝓞 K) K z` of the
principal idèles and the unipotent radicals `unipotentGL2 y`, and
`rationalCentreUnipotentQuotientMeasure K` the Haar-quotient measure on
`Z(K)U(K) \ AdelicGL2`.  This module computes that quotient measure in the **Iwasawa
coordinates** `z t k` (`z` a central-scalar representative modulo the principal idèles, `t`
a diagonal one-parameter torus element, `k` in the maximal compact `adelicMaximalCompact`)
of the principal-ideal fundamental domain `D`:

there is `c : ℝ≥0∞` with `c ≠ 0`, `c ≠ ∞` such that for every measurable fundamental
domain `D` of the principal idèles and every measurable `f` right-invariant under
`rationalCentreUnipotent K`,

  `∫⁻ q, f q.out ∂(rationalCentreUnipotentQuotientMeasure K)
     = c * ∫⁻ z in D, ∫⁻ t, ∫⁻ k, f (z·t·k) * ‖t‖⁻¹ ∂k ∂t ∂z`,

i.e. a constant (the product of the Iwasawa normalisation and the box volume) times the
iterated integral in the Iwasawa decomposition, weighted by the inverse idèle norm of the
torus coordinate.  This is the measure-theoretic Iwasawa decomposition the Rankin–Selberg
unfolding consumes: the `z`-integral is the principal-idèles quotient, the `t`-integral is
the `S`-part torus with its modulus weight `‖t‖⁻¹`, and the `k`-integral is the
probability measure `maximalCompactHaar`.

The proof is the quotient-measure computation `lintegral q, f q.out ∂quot = ∫ g, f g *
ρ g ∂g` with `ρ = HaarQuotient.density`, the adèlic Iwasawa disintegration
(`exists_lintegral_adelicGLHaar_eq_mul_lintegral_iwasawa`), the Haar-quotient Fubini and
density identities (`MeasureTheory/HaarQuotient{Fubini,Density}.lean`), and the `S`-part
measure algebra of the torus (`NumberTheory/NumberField/IdeleSPartIntegral.lean`).

References (public mirror, pinned):
<https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b3/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_lintegral_rationalCentreUnipotentQuotientMeasure_eq_mul_setLIntegral_iwasawa.lean>

spec-pin: Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_lintegral_rationalCentreUnipotentQuotientMeasure_eq_mul_setLIntegral_iwasawa.lean
spec-pin: P2M/Sol/S_AutomorphicForm_exists_lintegral_rationalCentreUnipotentQuotientMeasure_eq_mul_setLIntegral_iwasawa.lean

